# Compose-level env for Daimon's host sidecars (docker-compose.yml). Copy to .env only
# if you need to override; the sidecars run without it. Hermes runtime secrets are
# separate — see config/.env.example (seeded into ~/.hermes/.env).
#
# Miniflux (optional feeds source) lives on your shared infra stack, with its own
# admin credentials and Postgres. Daimon's `feeds` adapter consumes it at
# host.docker.internal:8930 (or miniflux:8080 on `shared`); set MINIFLUX_* in
# ~/.hermes/.env per config/.env.example.
#
# Observability (Grafana/Loki/Prometheus + alerting → Telegram) lives on your shared
# stack too; its monitoring TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN / TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID alert vars belong there.
# The telemetry sidecars here (chat-shipper, status-exporter) need no env.
